  <p><strong>Page transitions.</strong> This site's pages slide in the direction of navigation: <code>connectAstroTransitions()</code>, from <code>@udixio/motion/astro</code>, gives Astro's router that direction. Any other router can call <code>navigate(update, &#123; direction &#125;)</code>, which runs its update inside a View Transition.</p>

  <h2 id="demo-text">Text</h2>
  <p>A definition with <code>split</code> cuts the text of its element into <code>words</code> or <code>chars</code> (letters), and each piece plays the keyframes in a cascade, in the order of the text. A screen reader reads the text once, as written: the pieces are a visual copy that it skips. The heading is revealed word by word as it scrolls into view. The line below is written letter by letter, and Replay plays it out and in again.</p>
  <div class="not-prose flex flex-col gap-6">
